The robot will listen to audio the same way it is laid out in the Initial Architecture Document.

The omnidirectional microphone on the PYNQ board will be used to communicate with the bot.
An external microphone may be needed when playing to determine the direction of the noise.

When seeking, the MPR will look in one direction, say "Marco", and listen for the user's response.
If a response is not picked up, it will turn 45-90 degrees and try again.
When a response is heard, it will drive towards the response, going around objects if necessary.

When hiding, MPR will listen for "Marco" and reply "Polo"
